WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:02.168
-So happy to have you here.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.203 size:88% position:44%
-Great to be here, Seth.
-Absolutely delighted.

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.738 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want to get
to your new film,

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
but can we talk about
"In Bruges" just a little bit?

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We certainly can.
I hear you kind of like it

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
a little bit.
-I´m a little weird about

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:12.345
"In Bruges." I´m so --
I talk about "In Bruges" so much

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:15.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
that people have gifted me
"In Bruges" posters.

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.150
That´s right outside my office.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that --
I see your name everyday.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.620
-I´ve never seen that poster.
-You´ve never seen that poster?

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, that was --
It was a knockoff poster.

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
You didn´t get
any residuals for it.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:26.793
Someone just brought me --
bought me a big copperplate

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
that said "Bruges" on it,
so this is a movie

00:00:28.795 --> 00:00:29.829
I talk about all the time.
-That´s got to be heavy.

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is heavy, yeah.
Did you --

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.401 size:84% position:42%
So that movie, I guess,
came out in 2007, yes?

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:36.569 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And Colin Farrell,

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:37.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
Brenden Gleeson.

00:00:37.604 --> 00:00:39.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you look back
on that film fondly?

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:40.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, very much.

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:43.376 size:88% position:44%
My first feature film,
and, like, I didn´t know

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:47.247
what the hell I was doing,
but Colin and Brenden kind of

00:00:47.247 --> 00:00:49.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
guided me through it,
and it was --

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:51.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were in Bruges,
which is, as you know,

00:00:51.184 --> 00:00:53.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the most beautiful
and boring towns

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
in all of Europe.

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:55.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that --
It is interesting because

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:58.825
it is a balance of beauty
and not being very big.

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You spent a lot of time there

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:02.796 size:75% position:38%
because of the film.
-I went there, like,

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:04.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
maybe a couple years
before I wrote the script,

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:07.634 size:84% position:42%
and it all just popped
into my head instantly,

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:09.402
pretty much,
and I was kind of really worried

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:11.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
that someone else would make
a film in Bruges

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
before I got to,
and steal my thunder.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:15.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That´s really funny because
not only did they not,

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.910
but no one has made one since.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.679 size:84% position:42%
-And funnily enough,
no one ever went to see

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.247 size:84% position:42%
the movie, either so --

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:22.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:25.085
-Well, it´s interesting,
because I went to Bruges.

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:28.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
After the film,
my wife and I went to Bruges.

00:01:28.788 --> 00:01:31.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they -- the taxi driver
immediately clocked me

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
as an American tourist
who came because of the film.

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:37.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
So there is like a film
"In Bruges" tourism in Bruges.

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.466
-Oh, really?
-Do you feel like the Bruges --

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:41.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
the people of Bruges are happy
that you made the film?

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:44.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do they like it?
-I´ve never really been back

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
to check.
-Yeah.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:50.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I think the mayor --
No, I think the mayor

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
didn´t like it, so maybe --
-Oh, really?

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.781
I can´t believe they´re --
´Cause see, I want to do an

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.382
"In Bruges" reunion episode.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I heard this.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:01:59.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I´d like to --
-You would do it?

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:01.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If you want your
viewing figures to really dip,

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:03.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
that would be the perfect - -
-No, I think that NBC

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:05.291 size:84% position:42%
will be really excited
about "In Bruges" week.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:08.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:11.397
But so, this film, you know,
again, because I feel like

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
you are such a great writer
for actors,

00:02:13.733 --> 00:02:15.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this film,
Frances McDormand,

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:17.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
who we saw in the clip --
absolutely fantastic.

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:19.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you write this character
with her in mind?

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, this is completely
for Frances, like,

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:23.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
she´s one of
the best actors around,

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I´d always wanted
to work with her

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:26.346 size:75% position:38%
for years and years.

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:27.780
We met after a play in New York

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.250
about almost 20 years ago.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
-And then we met again,

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:34.621
like, seven or eight years ago,
and she said,

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:36.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Write a part for me."
-Oh, wow.

00:02:36.656 --> 00:02:38.925 size:81% position:41%
-And you always obey
when Frances tells you

00:02:38.925 --> 00:02:42.662
to do something, so that´s where
this film came about.

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And she is
a very unique character,

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
a very unique look
from the clip,

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:50.837
sort of the coveralls and the --
you know, the stuff in her hair.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:53.072
Is that a look that you had
in mind from the beginning?

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you guys work
on that together?

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:57.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that was pretty much
Frances´ idea.

00:02:57.944 --> 00:03:00.780
She plays a character who´s kind
of going to war with the town

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.015 size:75% position:38%
and with the police.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:04.617
So she wanted a uniform
that she wouldn´t have to

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:05.752 size:81% position:41%
think about every day.

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:07.020
She wasn´t going to coordinate,

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.088
like, a blouse with a dress.

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:12.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
So she´s got this kind of
mechanics uniform,

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:15.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a bandana,
but we wanted a hairstyle

00:03:15.428 --> 00:03:17.530
that would kind of match.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
And at one point,
we were thinking of getting,

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, a skinhead.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:24.437 size:81% position:41%
-And we did a kind of
computerized composite

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:28.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
of Frances with a skinhead
crew cut kind of thing,

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:30.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it didn´t quite -- yeah.
-No, yeah.

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:33.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We would have had
even less viewers

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:35.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
for this movie as "Bruges."
-Sub-Bruges?

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:37.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
You think you would
have gone sub-Bruges?

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:39.886
-Yeah, if that´s possible.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:42.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
But -- And, yeah,
but she did have,

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, a little --
if you see the film,

00:03:43.623 --> 00:03:45.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
she´s kind of got it shaved
in the back,

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.392
but the rest is swept up.

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:48.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it´s a pretty cool
iconic look she´s got going.

